        "error": null,
        "summary": "Implemented order state transitions in stockflow/main.py:\n\n1. **POST /orders/{id}/confirm**: Transitions PENDING -> CONFIRMED. Returns 409 INVALID_ORDER_STATE for any other state. No stock changes.\n\n2. **POST /orders/{id}/ship**: Transitions CONFIRMED -> SHIPPED. Returns 409 INVALID_ORDER_STATE for any other state. No stock changes.\n\n3. **POST /orders/{id}/cancel**: Transitions PENDING or CONFIRMED -> CANCELED. Restores stock for all order items. Returns 409 INVALID_ORDER_STATE for SHIPPED or CANCELED states.\n\nKey design decisions:\n- All endpoints use `lock=True` (SELECT FOR UPDATE) for optimistic concurrency control, ensuring only one valid transition succeeds in case of concurrent operations.\n- Stock restoration only happens on cancel (not on confirm/ship), and only once per cancel operation.\n- Tenant isolation is maintained through the existing `load_order` helper which filters by `tenant_id`.\n- The existing contract and tenant boundaries are preserved.",
